# Testing

## Context

Tests are colocated (`app/src/reducer.test.ts` next to `reducer.ts`) and run
with **vitest** (`cd app && npm test`) — see `app/src/reducer.test.ts` for the
existing style.

## Rule

- New test files are **colocated**: `foo.ts` gets `foo.test.ts` in the same
  directory, not a separate `__tests__`/`test/` tree.
- Use **vitest** APIs (`describe`, `it`, `expect`, `vi`) — the same imports
  already used in `app/src/reducer.test.ts`/`app/src/store.test.ts`. Do not
  introduce jest, mocha, or another test runner.
- Structure each test as **Arrange-Act-Assert**: set up input/state, perform
  the one action/call under test, assert the result — avoid interleaving
  setup and assertions.
- Match the existing naming style: `describe` names the unit under test
  (`"reducer"`, `"createStore"`, `"slugify"`); `it` names read as a plain-
  English behavior statement in lowercase, third person present tense
  ("adds a task as not done"), not "should add a task".
- Every new `Action` variant or exported function gets at least one happy-
  path test AND one edge case (empty input, missing id, boundary value) — one
  test per unit is not enough on its own.
- No snapshot tests — none exist in this codebase; assert on specific values/
  shapes instead (`toEqual`, `toBe`, `toHaveLength`), matching every existing
  test.

## How to verify

1. `cd app && npm test` is green.
2. Every new/changed `.ts`/`.tsx` file under `app/src` (excluding `types.ts`,
   `store.ts`) has a colocated `*.test.ts` covering it.
3. `grep -rnE "from ['\"]vitest['\"]" app/src` finds the vitest imports
   (either quote style), and `grep -rnE "from ['\"](jest|mocha|chai)['\"]"
   app/src` returns no matches — new test files import from `vitest`, never
   `jest`/`mocha`/`chai`.
4. `grep -rn "toMatchSnapshot" app/src` returns no matches.
5. Each new `it(...)` block name does not start with "should".